  "prefLabel": "Bea 502.31 Local governing body",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Bea 502.31 “Local governing body” means “local governing body” as defined in RSA 672:6, namely, “in addition to any other appropriate title:\n\nI. Board of selectmen in a town;\n\nII. City council or board of aldermen in a city;\n\nIII. Village district commissioners in a village district; or\n\nIV. County commissioners in a county in which there are located unincorporated towns or unorganized places.”\n\nSource. #14043, eff 8-8-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/bea500.html"
